dashboard.definition:
{
	"title": "Security Resilience",
	"description": "Firewall, identity, XDR, IDS/IPS, DNS, endpoint, threats",
	"inputs": {
		"input_global_trp": {
			"options": {
				"defaultValue": "-4h@m,now",
				"token": "global_time"
			},
			"title": "",
			"type": "input.timerange"
		}
	},
	"defaults": {
		"dataSources": {
			"ds.search": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			},
			"ds.spl2": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			}
		},
		"tokens": {
			"default": {}
		}
	},
	"visualizations": {
		"viz_about_bg": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeOpacity": 1,
				"strokeWidth": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_about_purpose": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "# Security Resilience\n\nCentralized view of **security posture** across firewalls, identity services, and threat intelligence. Use this dashboard to validate that defenses are holding, investigate anomalies, and prioritize response to active threats.\n\n**Audience:** Security Operations, Identity & Access Management, IT Leadership\n**Primary Sources:** Cisco ASA / FTD (Firewall), Cisco ISE, Active Directory, XDR / SecureX\n**Refresh:** All panels follow the global time picker; identity searches run every 15 minutes\n\n---\n\n## How to Navigate This Dashboard\n\n**Overview** — Firewall blocked/allowed traffic, ISE auth rates, AD lockouts, XDR incidents, and email security.\n*Start here — confirm perimeter defenses and identity services are operating normally.*\n\n**Details & KPI Reference** — Privileged user activity, failed logon analysis, account lockout trends, and identity event correlation.\n*Drill in when Overview shows elevated failures, lockouts, or unusual firewall patterns.*\n\n> **Reading pattern:** Stable blocked/allowed ratios and low failure counts = healthy. Spikes in blocked traffic, rising failed auth, or new lockout patterns = investigate on Details tab."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_about_sources": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#131a23",
				"fontColor": "#ecf0f5",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## Data Sources & Troubleshooting\n\n---\n\n**Cisco ASA / FTD** — Splunk Add-on for Cisco ASA\nSourcetypes: `cisco:asa`, `cisco:ftd`\nFreshness: Real-time (syslog)\n\n**Cisco ISE** — Cisco ISE Add-on for Splunk\nSourcetypes: `cisco:ise:syslog`\nFreshness: Real-time (syslog)\n\n**Active Directory** — Splunk Add-on for Windows\nSourcetypes: `WinEventLog:Security` (Event IDs 4672, 4625, 4740)\nFreshness: Real-time\n\n**Cisco Email Security** — Cisco Email Security Add-on\nSourcetypes: `cisco:esa:textmail`\nFreshness: ~5 min\n\n**XDR / SecureX** — Cisco SecureX Add-on\nSourcetypes: `cisco:securex:incidents`\nFreshness: ~15 min\n\n---\n\n**Panel showing \"No results\"?**\n\n1. **Widen the time range** — some metrics need 24+ hours of data\n2. **Verify the TAs are installed** — check *Manage Apps* for the add-ons listed above\n3. **Confirm data flow** — run `index=* sourcetype=cisco:asa | head 5` to test\n4. **Check saved search status** — verify scheduled searches are enabled\n\n---"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_box_events": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeOpacity": 1,
				"strokeWidth": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_fw": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#131a23",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(100,158,245,0.28)",
				"strokeOpacity": 1,
				"strokeWidth": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_ids_detail": {
